1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,900
If you run a personal injury law firm,
HVAC, roofing, or plumbing business,

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,160
your phone calls can be worth
thousands of dollars.

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:13,160
But what if Google Ads
isn't tracking all of them?

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:18,760
You might receive 30 serious calls,
while Google only sees 10 conversions.

5
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,380
Now Google thinks your campaign
is underperforming.

6
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,000
You cut the budget or pause the campaign,

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,620
when the campaign may actually be
bringing your best customers.

8
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,200
The problem may not be your ads.

9
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,640
Your tracking may be hiding
the real performance.

10
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:38,780
Here's the fix:

11
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:41,300
Track your calls properly.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,500
Identify which calls become qualified leads.

13
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:47,980
Then send those conversion signals
back to Google Ads.

14
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:52,300
When Google sees the leads
that actually matter,

15
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:58,440
it can optimize toward more qualified
customers and more revenue.

16
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:02,900
Otherwise, you may keep pausing
campaigns that are working

17
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,760
while your competitors
capture those customers.
